From: ProDefense LLC <legal@justtv.app>
Subject: [PATCH] access/file: avoid filesystem-volume inspection on Apple

JustTV passes app-local downloads or explicitly requested network media to
libVLC. Do not query mount flags through the disk-capacity API merely to
choose file read-ahead behavior. Treat Apple file descriptors as local;
HTTP/HLS/RTSP inputs retain their own network buffering paths.

This modification is offered under the same LGPL-2.1-or-later terms as
modules/access/file.c. Preserve this patch with the corresponding source.
It does not by itself qualify other modules or their privacy declarations.

--- a/modules/access/file.c
+++ b/modules/access/file.c
@@ -72,16 +72,11 @@
 static bool IsRemote (int fd)
 {
 #if defined(__APPLE__)
-    /* This has to preceed the general fstatvfs implmentation below,
-     * as even though Darwin has fstatvfs, it does not expose the
-     * MNT_LOCAL in the statvfs.f_flag field.
-     */
-    struct statfs sfs;
-
-    if (fstatfs (fd, &sfs))
-        return false;
-
-    return !((sfs.f_flags & MNT_LOCAL) == MNT_LOCAL);
+    /* JustTV modification: no volume-capacity API for a read-ahead hint.
+     * File inputs are app-local; network inputs use their access modules.
+     * Other platforms retain the upstream remote-filesystem behavior. */
+    (void)fd;
+    return false;
 
 #elif defined (HAVE_FSTATVFS) && defined (MNT_LOCAL)
     struct statvfs stf;
